(a) Definition. For the purpose of this section, the term "brown-bagging" means the consumption of any alcoholic beverage:
(1) On the premises of a business licensed to operate within the city, but not licensed for the consumption of such alcoholic beverage on the premises;
(2) By a customer or patron of such business;
(3) If the alcoholic beverage was not purchased from the business;
unless such consumption occurs during a private party held in a portion of the premises reserved for private parties, to which members of the general public are not admitted.
(b) Prohibited. Brown bagging is prohibited within the city.
(c) Exceptions. Nothing in this section shall be construed to prohibit the consumption of alcoholic beverages in a house, apartment, room or other premises designed and used for private residential occupancy.
(Ord. No. 2008-02, § 1(3-3), 3-3-2008)
